messages:    4%|3         | 22/600 [02:12<10:47,  1.12s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nA street comprehensive management committee has a total of 6 members: F, G, H, I, M and P. Each of these members shall serve as a member of at least one of the three sub-committees under the Comprehensive Management Committee. Each sub-committee consists of three different members. The known information is as follows: one of the six members serves as a member of three subcommittees. F is not a member of the same subcommittee as G. H is not a member of the same subcommittee as I.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options must be true?\n# Options:\nA) One of f or g is a member of three sub-committees.\nB) One of h or i is a member of three sub-committees.\nC) P or m is a member of only one sub-committee.\nD) One member happens to be a member of the two sub-committees.', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the given information and analyze it step by step:.\n\n1.**Total Members and Sub-committees**: There are 6 members (F, G, H, I, M, P) and 3 sub-committees, each consisting of 3 members.\n2.**One Member in Three Sub-committees**: One of the six members serves as a member of three sub-committees.\n3.**Constraints on Memberships**:.\n   - F is not a member of the same subcommittee as G.\n   - H is not a member of the same subcommittee as I.\n\nGiven these constraints, let's analyze the options:.\n\n**Option A: One of f or g is a member of three sub-committees.**.\n- We know that one member serves in three sub-committees.However, the context does not specify whether F or G is that member.Therefore, this option is not necessarily true.\n\n**Option B: One of h or i is a member of three sub-committees.**.\n- Unlike Option A, we have specific information confirming that either H or I is the member in three sub-committees. Hence, this option is indeed true.\n\n**Option C: P or m is a member of only one sub-committee.**.\n- We must verify if P or M can be a member of more than one sub-committee. Since one member is in three sub-committees, the remaining members can only be in one sub-committee each. If P or M is in more than one sub-committee, it would mean the other members are in one sub-committee each, which contradicts the given constraints. Therefore, this option is not a viable choice.\n\n**Option D: One member happens to be a member of the two sub-committees.**.\n- This option provides a clear and specific condition.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
