      "text": " A) The company will ensure that it can offer its employees any training necessary for meeting their job requirements.\n   - This option aligns with the context, as it acknowledges the need for continuous training to keep up with the rapid obsolescence of skills.\n   - Option B is not feasible because it suggests training only after five years, which is too late given the context that skills become obsolete within five years.\n   - Option C is not the best choice because increasing investment in AMT every year for five years might not be enough to keep up with the rapid obsolescence of skills. The context implies that skills become obsolete within five years, so a more immediate and continuous approach is needed.\n   - Option D is not the best choice because periodic surveys might not provide the necessary immediate training and support for employees to adapt to the changing skills.\n\n3.**Conclusion:**. The best plan for the company to prepare most effectively for the rapid obsolescence of skills is to ensure that it can offer its employees any training necessary for meeting their job requirements.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA\n</answer>",
