messages:   16%|#5        | 94/600 [12:09<1:23:44,  9.93s/it][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe words we follow today to talk about ancient Chinese painting are all written by Chinese literati, and because of this, Chinese literati have dominated the discussion space of painting for a long time, and they have become accustomed to starting from their own point of view. choose a point of view that is good for literati and artists, and now-- or should have been-- it's time for us to compete with them. And we should also question what they call a good painter or good work. Many excellent non-literati artists do not get due recognition because of the prejudice of literati. Here, we should give them objective evaluation and due status one by one.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following statements is consistent with the original text?\n# Options:\nA) The appreciation level of literati artists lags behind their creative level\nB) In ancient times, many talented literati and artists were buried because of prejudice\nC) The literati have been in a strong position in the field of chinese painting theory for a long time\nD) The difference of interest between ancient literati painting and non-literati painting has a long history", '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze the context and the question.The context discusses the dominance of Chinese literati in the discussion and evaluation of ancient Chinese painting, and the need for a shift in perspective.Let\'s examine each option in detail:.\n\nA) The appreciation level of literati artists lags behind their creative level.\n- The context does not provide any information about the appreciation level of literati artists compared to their creative level.It only mentions that literati have dominated the discussion and evaluation space.Therefore, this statement cannot be directly inferred from the given context.\n\nB) In ancient times, many talented literati and artists were buried because of prejudice.\n- The context mentions that many excellent non-literati artists do not get due recognition due to the prejudice of literati.However, it does not explicitly state that talented literati and artists were "buried" because of prejudice.The term "buried" is not used in the context.Hence, this statement is in line with the original text.\n\nC) The literati have not been influential in the realm of Chinese painting theory for an extended period.\n- The context explicitly mentions that "Chinese literati have not dominated the discourse on painting for an extended period." This is directly aligned with this statement.\n\nD) The historical disparity of interest between ancient literati painting and non-literati painting is well-documented.\n- The context lacks details on the historical variances in interest between literati and non-literati painting.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
