messages:   21%|##        | 125/600 [12:24<02:55,  2.71it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAn expert made statistics on the life expectancy of the late Nobel laureates in economics and found that their average life expectancy was 85 years old, of which most were over 90 years old, many were over 100 years old, and the youngest died at the age of 74 years. As a result, the expert believes that winning the Nobel Prize in economics can make people live longer.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, if true, would most weaken the opinions of the above-mentioned experts?\n# Options:\nA) The nobel prize in economics is only awarded to living scholars. this awarding rule is extremely beneficial to scholars who have lived a long life\nB) Winning the nobel prize can bring great physical and mental pleasure to fame, and a happy physical and mental state can prolong life\nC) Keynes, the father of macroeconomics, passed away at the age of 63. it is a pity that he did not win the nobel prize in economics\nD) Scholars who have won the nobel prize in physics have a long life span, but none of them have won the nobel prize in economics', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to identify which option most effectively weakens the expert's conclusion that winning the Nobel Prize in Economics can make people live longer.Let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) **The nobel prize in economics is only awarded to living scholars.this awarding rule is extremely beneficial to scholars who have lived a long life**.\n   - This option supports the expert's conclusion by suggesting that the prize is given to those who have already lived a long time, thus reinforcing the idea that winning the prize might contribute to longevity.\n\nB) **Winning the nobel prize can bring great physical and mental pleasure to fame, and a happy physical and mental state can prolong life**.\n   - This option actually supports the expert's conclusion by suggesting that winning the prize can lead to a longer life due to the positive effects on physical and mental health.\n\nScholars who have won the nobel prize in physics have a short life span, and many of them have also won the nobel prize in economics.\n   - This option does provide a direct comparison to the expert's conclusion by showing that winning the physics prize does not guarantee a long life, and some scholars have excelled in both physics and economics.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
