messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNearly all employees of the factory who have completed their high school diploma have earned their factory safety certificate, having easily completed the eight week training course. The high school graduates who haven' t earned the certificate are ones who have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the course. Overall, though, most of the factory workers have not earned the certificate.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if the statements above are true, which one of the following also must be true?\n# Options:\nA) A large proportion of the factory workers have not graduated from high school.\nB) A large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the eight week training course.\nC) Most of the workers who have earned the certificate are high school graduates.\nD) No factory worker without a high school diploma has completed the course and earned the certificate.", "<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the given context and analyze each option step by step.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**\n   - Nearly all employees who have completed high school have earned the factory safety certificate.\n   - High school graduates who haven't earned the certificate are those with evening obligations that prevented them from taking the course.\n   - Overall, most factory workers have not earned the certificate.\n\n2.**Option A: A large proportion of the factory workers have not graduated from high school.**\n   - The context does not provide any information about the proportion of workers who have not graduated from high school.It only mentions that high school graduates who haven't earned the certificate have evening obligations.Therefore, we cannot conclude that a large proportion of workers have not graduated from high school.\n\n3.**Option B: A large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the course.**\n   - The context states that high school graduates who haven't earned the certificate are those with evening obligations.However, it does not specify the proportion of high school graduates who have evening obligations.Therefore, we cannot conclude that a large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations.\n\nBased on the analysis, the only option that must be true given the context is Option D.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
