round collisions have been caused by the least experienced ground-crew members.".\n     - This option provides a reason for why the training might be effective but does not directly address the cost reduction aspect.\n   - **Option B:** "A ground collision typically occurs when there are no passengers on the airplane.".\n     - This option is irrelevant to the cost reduction argument and does not provide a logical link.\n   - **Option C:** "The additional training will focus on helping ground crews avoid those kinds of ground collisions that cause the most costly damage.".The least logical completion of the argument is Option C, as it indirectly avoids why the drop in repair costs can be expected to be much greater than the cost of the training.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
