messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nFor example, X X Group held an anniversary celebration, your mobile phone number won a grand prize of 100000 yuan. this kind of unwise fraudulent text messages on mobile phones still appear again and again even after they have been exposed by the media. Professional swindlers prefer to use shoddy fraudulent text messages rather than design more deceptive and gullible text messages, which only shows that the swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options, if true, strongly refutes the above conclusion?\n# Options:\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\nC) If a deception was useless, the swindler would have eliminated it long ago.\nD) Swindlers use such text messages to catch people who may be fooled, and they want to filter out smart people in the first place.', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze the context and the question.The context discusses the persistence of fraudulent text messages despite their exposure, and it concludes that swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional to design more deceptive messages.The question asks us to identify which option, if true, would strongly refute this conclusion.\n\nLet's examine each option:.\n\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\n- This option directly contradicts the conclusion that swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional.If swindlers must be smart to deceive others, then the conclusion that they are too stupid is false.This option strongly refutes the given conclusion.\n\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\n- This option does not directly address the intelligence or professionalism of swindlers.It only speaks to their behavior in avoiding detection.It does not challenge the idea that they are too stupid to design more deceptive messages.\nSwindlers intentionally send text messages to avoid fooling intelligent individuals, indicating their desire to target only gullible people.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
