't have children with type B blood.**.\n     - This option is not supported by the professor\'s statement.The professor\'s statement clearly states that it is impossible to have children with type B blood if one parent has type O blood.\n   - **Option C: People with type B blood will always have children with type O blood.**.\n     - This option is supported by the professor\'s statement. The professor\'s statement affirms that type B parents will always have type O children.\n   - **Option D: If both parents have type B blood, their children will also have type B blood.**.\n     - This option is supported by the professor\'s statement. The professor\'s statement indicates that if both parents have type B blood, their children will also have type B blood.\n\n4.**Conclusion:**.\n   - The student\'s statement supports the professor\'s clear statement about type O parents.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
