messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is closest to the meaning of the above judgement?\n# Options:\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\nC) If the truth is not shut out, then the door to all wrong must not be closed.\nD) To accept the truth, we must reject wrong.', '<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let\'s break down the given context and analyze each option step by step.\n\nThe context states: "If you close all the wrong doors, truth will be shut out.".\n\nThis statement can be rephrased in a more formal logical form:.\n- If P (closing all the wrong doors), then Q (truth will be shut out).\n\nWe need to find the option that best captures the meaning of this statement.\n\nLet\'s analyze each option:.\n\nA) If truth is shut out, it must be that you close all the wrong doors.\n- This option suggests a conditional statement: If Q (truth is shut out), then P (you close all the wrong doors).\n- This is the contrapositive of the original statement, but it does not directly capture the original meaning.\n\nB) Truth can not be shut out unless all the doors of wrong are closed.\nTo keep truth from being shut out, it\'s important to leave all the wrong doors open.\n- This is the opposite of the original statement, indicating that keeping wrong doors open ensures truth is not shut out.\n\nC) If truth is kept out, then all wrong doors should be closed.\n- This option implies that closing all wrong doors results in truth being kept out.\n- This is a different perspective and does not align with the original meaning.\n\nD) Embracing falsehood is crucial to embracing truth.\n- This option suggests that accepting falsehood leads to accepting truth, which contrasts with the original statement.\n- This is not in line with the original statement.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
