weakens the detective's argument because it indicates that the embezzlement was possible even if the embezzler was an accountant.\n\nB) There is evidence of breaches in computer security at the time of the embezzlement that could have given persons outside XYZ Corporation access to internal financial records.\n- This option introduces an alternative method of embezzlement that does not rely on the embezzler having internal access.If someone outside the company had access to the financial records, it weakens the detective's argument that the embezzler must have had specialized knowledge and access to internal records.XYZ Corporation employs only two accountants, whereas it has eight actuaries on its staff.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
