messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nWittgenstein was a student of Moore, a famous philosopher at Cambridge University. One day, philosopher Russell asked Moore, who is your best student? Moore said without hesitation: Wittgenstein. why? because among all the students, only he always showed a blank look when listening to the class, and there were always endless questions. later, Wittgenstein is more famous than Russell. Someone asked, why did Russell fall behind? Wittgenstein said: he has no problem.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, this paragraph is intended to illustrate that:\n# Options:\nA) Doubting and questioning are always the secret of success\nB) Curiosity is the internal driving force of research\nC) Appreciation is an important factor in success\nD) Finding problems is the premise of continuous progress', "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the context and analyze the key points:.\n\n1.**Context Summary**:.\n   - Wittgenstein was a student of Moore.\n   - Moore was asked by Russell who was his best student.\n   - Moore's response was Wittgenstein.\n   - Wittgenstein was later more famous than Russell.\n   - Russell asked Wittgenstein why he was more famous, and Wittgenstein said he had no problem.\n\n2.**Core of the Question**:.\n   - The question asks what the paragraph is intended to illustrate based on the given information.\n\n3.**Analyzing the Options**:.\n   - **Option A: Doubting and questioning are always the secret of success**.\n     - This option suggests that questioning is the key to success.However, the context doesn't explicitly state that questioning is the secret to success.It only mentions Wittgenstein's questioning and curiosity.\n   - **Option B: Curiosity is the internal driving force of research**.The paragraph suggests that curiosity and questioning are not important traits for success or research, contradicting the conclusion drawn from the context.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
