ids decreases, and their temperature changes less dramatically.\n- This option suggests that as people age, their body fluids contain less water, leading to less dramatic temperature changes.However, it does not address why heat stroke is more likely in young children in a car.\nHeat stroke typically happens when you gain weight in water. Young children with a smaller body surface area absorb heat slowly, and because they have fewer sweat glands than adults, they retain water more efficiently.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
