messages:   98%|#########7| 586/600 [25:23<00:03,  4.26it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nWhen you are about to graduate, a certain class will select outstanding graduates, and discussions are ongoing within the class. Class leader: Either Li Xue is rated as an outstanding graduate or Wang Lei is rated as an outstanding graduate. Youth League Party Secretary: I disagree.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following accurately expresses the opinion of the party secretary?\n# Options:\nA) Both li xue and wang lei were rated as outstanding graduates\nB) Neither li xue nor wang lei can be rated as outstanding graduates\nC) Either li xue and wang lei are both rated as outstanding graduates, or neither li xue nor wang lei can be rated as outstanding graduates\nD) Li xue was rated as an outstanding graduate, wang lei cannot be rated as an outstanding graduate', '<think>\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, we need to carefully analyze the statements made by the class leader and the Youth League Party Secretary.Let\'s break it down step by step.\n\n1.**Class Leader\'s Statement:**\n   - The class leader asserts that either Li Xue or Wang Lei is rated as an outstanding graduate.This can be represented in logical terms as:\n     \\[\n     L \\lor W\n     \\]\n     where \\( L \\) represents "Li Xue is rated as an outstanding graduate" and \\( W \\) represents "Wang Lei is rated as an outstanding graduate."\n\n2.**Youth League Party Secretary\'s Statement:**\n   - The Youth League Party Secretary disagrees with the class leader.This means the Secretary\'s statement must contradict the class leader\'s statement.The Secretary\'s disagreement can be interpreted as:\n     \\[\n     \\neg (L \\lor W)\n     \\]\n     which is equivalent to:\n     \\[\n     \\neg L \\land \\neg W\n     \\]\n     This means both Li Xue and Wang Lei cannot be rated as outstanding graduates.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct option that accurately expresses the opinion of the Youth League Party Secretary is: Option A: Both Li Xue and Wang Lei were rated as outstanding graduates.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
